{"event_type":"review","id":"9079e2f9f89cb01d5ab2ec4d01165caba442a433ba726d4249cf8be30af3ff7f","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T13:50:36Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/df18f7635cb2505b9bcfd9c4321588830438b123f73d9dd91f6515e0e0f55929","sha256":"df18f7635cb2505b9bcfd9c4321588830438b123f73d9dd91f6515e0e0f55929"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/4943a1e7875404386121d4d1b4ebafb81bf01112117a8872cdaa5699a1d70d5c","sha256":"4943a1e7875404386121d4d1b4ebafb81bf01112117a8872cdaa5699a1d70d5c"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/88193e7c410555fc70b32fe8de7c3a4864840694833af5378979ddcb6a119746","sha256":"88193e7c410555fc70b32fe8de7c3a4864840694833af5378979ddcb6a119746"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6dbe29f4bd4a1088b1f73fec47f53f3af70ef9ac2592a33a311e190cb33ecd76","sha256":"6dbe29f4bd4a1088b1f73fec47f53f3af70ef9ac2592a33a311e190cb33ecd76"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/33dc42dc6725269b7667c85353d415697c0213fc5e4cffaa76817e7d8cc1e77c","sha256":"33dc42dc6725269b7667c85353d415697c0213fc5e4cffaa76817e7d8cc1e77c"}],"attempt_id":"3a3d9c2ddbce01b386067b9bcf61f2eee90a7c6a6941913c0291989a7d1c7e4e:0:1","base":"a61a44805b0091fb21ce9d36b2ea9b7391f254af","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"7539ff30498413a5d3cb166ef61e130dc1b1c3bd","body":"**Stop the authority scan at `/` before searching for userinfo.**\n\nIn `canonicalRepoPath` at Line 239-243, the scan stops only at whitespace, `?` or `#`. As a result, `authority` contains the whole path. `lastIndexOf('@')` at Line 245 then matches any `@` in the path, not only a userinfo `@`.\n\n- `https://github.com/org/repo@v1` rewrites to `https://v1`.\n- `host = \"v1\"` and `path = \"\"`.\n- `https://other.example/x/y@v1` gives the same repoId.\n\nTwo different repositories then share one archive identity, and the result drops the real host. The text before that `@` is still removed, so no credential leaks. A URL userinfo cannot contain an unencoded `/` (RFC 3986), so ending the authority at the first `/` keeps the \"last `@`\" rule for passwords that contain `@`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     while (end < rest.length) {\n       const ch: string | undefined = rest[end];\n-      if (ch === undefined || /\\s/.test(ch) || ch === '?' || ch === '#') break;\n+      if (ch === undefined || /\\s/.test(ch) || ch === '/' || ch === '?' || ch === '#') break;\n       end++;\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\nThe OpenGrep `exec` hints at Line 235, Line 252, Line 259 and Line 266 are false positives. Those calls are `RegExp.prototype.exec`, not `child_process`.","id":"adc33b40e4961b44d121d1b12d44202acd059ab64c3d805324eae042140920df","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/fix/attemptRecord.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Stop the authority scan at `/` before searching for userinfo."}],"head":"4b887d697a7824db1f33157ae1e6fc9d448bb2c7","head_tree":"a619b07177492e5c80d4ce45880731ec409f8b2c","input_scope":[{"blob":"7539ff30498413a5d3cb166ef61e130dc1b1c3bd","intervals":[[1,476]],"path":"src/ops/fix/attemptRecord.ts"},{"blob":"493c6ada59bbfe8dd8de8fa64cbdccb47a2f3eec","intervals":[[1,95]],"path":"src/ops/fix/correlation.ts"},{"blob":"2507b129055790a96408e70dd9866c4cdc84dd23","intervals":[[1,345]],"path":"src/ops/fix/measurement.ts"},{"blob":"d12f35d61353c2b9a85977e46f16100c38a997b1","intervals":[[1,490]],"path":"src/ops/fix/reportFold.ts"}],"job_id":"3a3d9c2ddbce01b386067b9bcf61f2eee90a7c6a6941913c0291989a7d1c7e4e:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"7539ff30498413a5d3cb166ef61e130dc1b1c3bd","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/fix/attemptRecord.ts","reason":"boun